# How to add your own tutorial

Tutorials are written as plain Doxygen files and typically have the extension dox.
If you prefer to have Python notebooks, please store the notebook (without any 
binary content) in the repo. The notebooks then have to be converted before we 
actually invoke doxygen. This is done through the following steps per notebook
file:

- Invoke
  ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
jupyter nbconvert --to markdown tutorials/exahype2/exercises/swe/swe.ipynb
  ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
  It is important that you stay within the directory hosting tutorials, as 
  follow-up steps will use this information to construct some file handles.
- Call the Peano-specific postprocessing script on this file:  
  ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
python3 tutorials/postprocess-markdown-of-jupyter-notebook.py tutorials/exahype2/exercises/swe/swe
  ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
  Note that we omit the extension here.
- Remove the converted md file:
  ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
rm tutorials/exahype2/exercises/swe/swe.md
  ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
  This is important as we otherwise will get garbage.
  
If you now call Doxygen, the notebook is integrated into the static webpage.
It will be given the identifier that corresponds to the qualified file path, 
where all / are replaced with underscores.




*/

